              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Juno Vale grew up in Rockford, Illinois, playing church organ on Sundays and her brother's synthesizers the rest of the week. She moved to Chicago at nineteen and spent five years playing keys in other people's bands before releasing the Night Shift EP in 2021."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Her debut album Paper Moons (2023) was made in a bedroom on Kedzie Avenue and found its way onto late-night radio across the Midwest. Afterglow, her second album, was recorded live to tape with a four-piece band and has taken her on her first headline tour of North America and Europe."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          "column": 1,
          "variant": "default"
        },
        {
          "id": "blk_kfqd896ak9",
          "type": "button",
          "v": 1,
          "fields": {
            "label": "Download the press kit",
            "link": {
              "type": "url",
              "url": "https://junovale.example/press-kit.zip"
            },
            "role": "secondary"
          },
          "column": 1,
          "variant": "default"
        }
      ]
